<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds drifted higher in cautious afternoon trade on Tuesday as dealers awaited the outcome of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy setting Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) meeting.</p>
<p>Analysts widely expect the FOMC to sanction a 25 basis point hike in its Fed funds rate, and dealers said this had largely been factored into the market.</p>
<p>&quot;I don't know what would happen if they didn't raise rates,&quot; said one dealer. &quot;The truth is that the market is simply not prepared for that outcome.&quot;</p>
</text>
